Borehole Velvet

Ingredients: NU JAZZ / ELECTRO JAZZ + COZY, WARM & CHILL LO-FI + 808 + 1980s ERA
Creative Catalyst: Invented two kilometers underground by copper miners who transformed pressurized galvanized ventilation ducts into resonant polyrhythmic percussion rigs.

Borehole Velvet sounds like an illicit, velvet-lined jazz speakeasy carved directly into a sweltering salt-and-copper deposit. Cavernous, low-passed Roland TR-808 sub-bass mimics tectonic plate shifts beneath swung, dust-crusted lo-fi cassette grooves; glassy 1980s Yamaha DX7 FM bells and lush Rhodes MK-I chords drift through the gloom, while Harmon-muted brass cries float over the hypnotic, metallic clinking of miners rhythmically striking tuned air ducts with brass spanners.

